    "reference": {
      "name": "3-D vortex lattice on the camber surface, strip-coupled to the 2-D Hess-Smith panel solution, Prandtl-Glauert compressibility",
      "citation": "Hess & Smith (1967); Moran, An Introduction to Theoretical and Computational Aerodynamics (1984) ch. 4 and 7; Katz & Plotkin, Low-Speed Aerodynamics (2001) ch. 12 (vortex lattice); Prandtl (1927) / Glauert (1928) compressibility rule",
      "assumptions": [
        "attached potential flow: no separation, no shock, no boundary layer, no viscous drag",
        "Prandtl-Glauert is the linearised compressible rule, so the transonic answer is the subsonic one stretched by 1/beta; the drag divergence the Korn rule would flag is not in the field",
        "the section solve is 2-D and sees only the local lift the lattice gives it, so spanwise flow inside the boundary layer is absent",
        "rigid wing: no aeroelastic twist",
        "chord 1 m, free stream 1 m/s, incompressible section"
      ],
